      "marks": 30,
      "question": [
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257900",
          "text": "<p>When a $2$-input NOR gate has all its input lines and output line inverted, it becomes:</p>\n\n<ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>NAND gate</li>\n    <li>EXNOR gate</li>\n    <li>EXOR gate</li>\n    <li>OR gate</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1,digital-logic,digital-circuits",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257893",
          "text": "<p>The number of minterms in an expression for $n$-input Ex-NOR gate can be given by:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$2^{\\frac{n^2}{2}}$</li>\n    <li>$\\frac{2^{n}}{2}$</li>\n    <li>$\\frac{n^2}{2}$</li>\n    <li>$n$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257891",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is/are true?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>AND gate resembles switches in parallel while OR gate resembles switches in series connection.</li>\n    <li>AND gate resembles switches in series while OR gate resembles switches in parallel connection.</li>\n    <li>AND gate resembles switches in series while NOR gate resembles switches in parallel connection.</li>\n    <li>AND gate resembles switches in parallel while NOR gate resembles switches in series connection.</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257889",
          "text": "The minimum number of at most 2-input gates (AND, OR and NOT gates) required to realize following expression is________\n\n$\\overline{a}.  \\overline{(\\overline{a}\\overline{b}+\\overline{(a+c)})}$",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "3",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257887",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following expression represents the Boolean function shown in k-map below:</p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" style=\"width:300px\">\n    <tbody>\n        <tr>\n            <td>$A$</td>\n            <td>$B$</td>\n            <td>$f(A, B)$</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>$0$</td>\n            <td>$0$</td>\n            <td>$1$</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>$0$</td>\n            <td>$1$</td>\n            <td>$D$</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>$1$</td>\n            <td>$0$</td>\n            <td>$1$</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>$1$</td>\n            <td>$1$</td>\n            <td>$D$</td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$\\text{OR gate}$</li>\n    <li>$\\text{AND gate}$</li>\n    <li>$\\overline{B}$</li>\n    <li>$1$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257885",
          "text": "<p>A three variable Boolean function is defined as $f(A,B,C)=\\sum \\{0,1,6,7\\}$. If $\\overline{f(A,B,C)}$ is defined as complement of $f(A,B,C)$ then the simplified expression for $\\overline{f(A,B,C)}$ can be given by:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$B \\oplus C$</li>\n    <li>$1$</li>\n    <li>$A\\odot B$</li>\n    <li>$A\\oplus B$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257883",
          "text": "<p>The Gray code representation of $117_{10}$ is:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$1111001$</li>\n    <li>$1001111$</li>\n    <li>$1110110$</li>\n    <li>$1110101$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257881",
          "text": "When all inputs to a logic circuit are high, still the output is low, then the gate can be:<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  either Ex-OR or NAND but not NOR<br /> </li><li>  either Ex-NOR or NAND but not NOR<br /> </li> <li> either Ex-OR or NOR but not NAND<br /> </li>  <li> none of the above  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257879",
          "text": "<p>Consider the K-map shown below with four variables where, “D” denotes don’t care states.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"GATEBOOK-2019-DL1-9\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>\n\n<p>The number of Essential Prime implicants in the K-map shown above is______</p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "1",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257877",
          "text": "<p>What happens when a bit-string of length $m-bit$ is Ex-NORed with itself n-times as shown: $[(B \\odot (B \\odot (B \\odot (B....\\text{n times}]$&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>complements when n is even</li>\n    <li>complements when n is odd</li>\n    <li>produces $2^m-1$ when n is even</li>\n    <li>remains unchanged when n is even</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257875",
          "text": "Logical Ex-NOR operation (of two variables A and B) is equivalent to which of the following set expressions?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  $(A \\cup B)-(A \\cap B)$<br /> </li><li>  $(1- (A \\cap B) )$<br /> </li> <li> $(1-(A \\cup B)- (A \\cap B))$<br /> </li>  <li> $(1-(A \\cup B)) \\cup (A \\cap B)$  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257873",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following is equivalent to following Boolean expression:<br>\n$\\overline{D} + (\\overline{A}B\\overline{C} + A\\overline{B}.\\overline{C})D + AC\\overline{D} + \\overline{(\\overline{A}\\oplus 0).A}$</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$D$</li>\n    <li>$\\overline{D}$</li>\n    <li>$0$</li>\n    <li>$(B+\\overline{B}D+\\overline{B}\\overline{D})$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257871",
          "text": "<p>Minimum number of NOR gates required to realize following Boolean function is:<br>\n$f(A,B,C) = AB + \\overline{C}$</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$3$</li>\n    <li>$4$</li>\n    <li>$5$</li>\n    <li>$6$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257869",
          "text": "<p>Consider the K-map shown below with four variables.<br>\n<img alt=\"GATEBOOK-2019-DL1-14\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>\n\n<p>The value of multiplication of the number of prime implicants and number of Essential Prime implicants in the K-map shown above is________</p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "15",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1,numerical-answers",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257867",
          "text": "<p>The output $Y$ in the circuit shown below, is always $1$ when:<br>\n<img alt=\"GATEBOOK-2019-DL1-15\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Odd number of inputs are $1$</li>\n    <li>Even number of inputs are $0$</li>\n    <li>At least $2$ of the inputs are $1$</li>\n    <li>At least $1$ of the inputs are $1$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257865",
          "text": "<p>The gray code for a decimal number $N$ is $11111111_2$. This number $N$ is converted into $P$ which belongs to $8$ &nbsp;$4$ &nbsp;$-2$ &nbsp;$-1$ code system. What is the Hexadecimal representation for P?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$ABC$</li>\n    <li>$F55$</li>\n    <li>$170$</li>\n    <li>$790$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257863",
          "text": "<p>The four variable function f is given as collection of sum-of-product terms as follows:<br>\n$f(A,B,C,D) = \\{2,3,8,10,11,12,14,15\\}$<br>\nWhich of the following correctly represents the pair (P,Q) where P represents the minimized expression for this function and Q stands for minimum number of two input NAND gates required to realize this function, considering variables are available only in their nonprime form:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$A\\overline{D}+AC+\\overline{B}C, \\: 6$</li>\n    <li>$A\\overline{C}+AD+\\overline{B}C, \\: 8$</li>\n    <li>$A\\overline{D}+AC+\\overline{B}C, \\: 8$</li>\n    <li>$A\\overline{C}+AD+\\overline{B}C, \\: 6$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257861",
          "text": "<p>Given function $f_1$, $f_2$ and $f_3$ as follows:<br>\n$f_1 = \\sum m \\{2,3,4,5\\}$<br>\n$f_2 = \\sum m \\{1,2,3,4,6\\}$<br>\n$f_3 = \\sum m \\{1,3,5,6\\}$</p>\n\n<p>and the logic circuit shown below:<br>\n<img alt=\"GATEBOOK-2019-DL1-18\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\">Which of the following collection of minterms best represents the function $f$?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$\\sum m\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\sum m\\{2,3,4,5,6\\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\sum m\\{1,3,4,5,6\\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\sum m\\{1,2,3,4,6\\}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257859",
          "text": "<p>If decimal value of $(402)_y$ is $7_{10}$ less than that of &nbsp;$(173)_x$ then possible values of $x$ and $y$ in octal number system respectively are:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$11,16$</li>\n    <li>$15,9$</li>\n    <li>$9,12$</li>\n    <li>$17,11$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "257857",
          "text": "<p>Consider the $16$-bit floating-point format which has $9$ rightmost bits for the mantissa and $6$ bits for the excess-$31$ exponent (base $2$) in the middle and most significant bit stands for sign of the float number. Which of the following represents the difference between the smallest and third smallest normalized positive float value (using implicit leading 1) in this system?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$2^{-39}$</li>\n    <li>$2^{-35}$</li>\n    <li>$2^{-38}$</li>\n    <li>$2^{-32}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-dl1,floating-point-representation",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}